          "message": "Move README images off Cloudinary (#22160)\n\n* Store README images in the repo instead of loading them from Cloudinary\n\nAdd the Node.js / Python / Go / Bash icons to images/languages/ and point\nthe root and GitHub component READMEs at them, and point the Discord Bot\nREADME at the bot_priviledges.png already committed next to it (identical\nto the Cloudinary copy).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Serve component README images from assets.pipedream.net\n\nPoint the 149 remaining Cloudinary image references across 30 component\nREADMEs at byte-identical copies in s3://assets.pipedream.net/s.v0/static/legacy/.\n\nTwo references stay: the Cloudinary integration's own demo-account URL\n(cloudinary.app.mjs) and a truncated, already-broken image link in the\nMongoDB README that has no recoverable URL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
